+# Monthly export without contact details (rework)
+
+Dana Okafor rejected `task-002-monthly-orders-csv-export` (commit 8425603): the accountant's export must not carry
+customers' email addresses or phone numbers; the order number, date, customer name and total only. This task reworks
+that change so it can be approved again.
+
+## What it asks for
+
+- The monthly export (`exportMonth`) carries only `order`, `date`, `customer` and `total`, as task-002 specifies.
+- No customer email address or phone number appears anywhere in the export text, whatever the customer's details.
+- The guarantee is pinned by a test, so a later change cannot bring the contact details back unnoticed.
+
+## Findings
+
+- The export code in `src/domain/orders.ts` already reads only the customer's name from the customer record; the
+  email address and phone number are never written to the CSV. A probe with two customers, each with an email and a
+  phone, gave rows with the order number, date, name and total only.
+- Nothing in the code changes for the export's output. The rework adds the regression test above, so the rule Dana
+  stated is checked by `npm test` rather than only by reading the code.
+
+## Choices
+
+- The rework adds a test rather than changing the export's output, because the output already meets the reason given.
+- The test checks the header-and-rows text for the customers' email addresses and phone numbers, not only the column
+  names, so a leak through the name column or a quoted field would also fail it.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- The export test for contact details passes, and `npm test` passes.
+- The export still gives the columns and values task-002 specifies.
+- README and CHANGELOG are unchanged for this rework; the export is documented in `README.md` as before.
